From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 23:57:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00694/11171] [outer-loop] Blog publish guard: standalone
 pre-push hook (no pre-commit stash)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Switch the guard from a pre-commit pre-push hook to a STANDALONE git pre-push
hook. pre-commit's pre-push dispatcher stashes unstaged files for the hook run,
which would put a stash window on the conductor's auto-push path — exactly what
CLAUDE.md "Never Stash — Always Commit-First" forbids. The standalone hook reads
committed SHAs only and never touches the working tree, so nothing is stashed.

  - scripts/git-hooks/pre-push: version-controlled hook source (runs the guard).
  - scripts/install-git-hooks.sh: installer (run once per clone; re-run if
    `pre-commit install --hook-type pre-push` ever clobbers it).
  - .pre-commit-config.yaml: removed the blog-publish-guard pre-commit entry,
    left a NOTE pointing at the standalone hook.
  - guard logic unchanged (scripts/blog_publish_guard.py); re-tested 4 ways via
    the raw stdin protocol (clean=allow, unapproved=block, allowlisted=allow,
    no-op=allow) + confirmed no stash on real hook invocation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
